# What Vercel does NOT need.
#
# The deployment serves docs/ as static HTML and runs one Python function,
# api/ask.py, which reaches egress.desk and egress.llm. Between them those read
# exactly two files: state/universe.json and state/symbol_marks.json, both
# already named by `includeFiles` in vercel.json.
#
# state/snapshots/ is the raw crawl archive - one gzipped CSV per day, growing
# by roughly 15 MB a day and never read at request time. It reached 209 MB and
# took the whole function bundle to 228.11 MB, over Vercel's limit, and every
# production deployment failed from 2026-09-28 02:47Z with "Total bundle size
# exceeds the maximum function size". Nothing about the site changed; the
# archive simply grew past the line.
#
# Do not add docs/ here. It is the outputDirectory, and excluding it would
# serve nothing.

.git
.github
tests
tools
state/snapshots
**/__pycache__
